peline, Not a Window: Information Attrition in LLM Agent Harnesses (Replication Package)", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23614755", "publication_date": "2026-10-24", "description": "<p>Anonymized replication package for an ICSE 2027 NIER submission (title above), currently under double-anonymous review. Contains the code and data behind the paper, not the paper manuscript itself.</p><p>The paper measures how much of a tool-using LLM agent's output is lost before the model ever sees it, in an agent that diagnoses injected faults from Linux kernel traces. It finds that a third of all tool results were destroyed in transit by a positional (prefix-slice) cut, and runs a registered, controlled experiment to test whether that cut causes the accuracy gap it correlates with.</p><p>Layout: <code>agent/</code> is the harness under study (the LangGraph diagnosis agent and its tool-result cutting mechanism); <code>study/</code> is everything specific to this paper -- drivers, derived results, the full replay corpus of raw transcripts, the delivery-cliff figure, and the registered pre-analysis plan with its dated amendment log. See the top-level README.md for the full layout and a verified reproduction guide (which scripts run standalone with no API key or raw trace data, and which need data available on request).</p><p>Not included: the raw multi-gigabyte LTTng/CTF kernel trace capture, available on request through the venue's anonymous channel.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Anonymous", "affiliation": null}], "keywords": ["LLM agents", "agent harnesses", "context engineering", "tool use", "replication package", "ICSE 2027 NIER", "kernel traces", "root cause analysis"], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23614754"}}]}, "notes": "Companion artifact for a submission currently under double-anonymous review. 